WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:03.370
If you want to hear by theory on how a couple
of familiar characters might have played a

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.540
hand in the ending of Annabelle Comes Home,
then stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.920
It’s been a long journey spanning over several
movies, but Annabelle is finally coming home.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:21.080
Today on Things You Missed I’m covering
the third movie of the Annabelle subset, Annabelle

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.080
Comes Home.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.080
And it starts with the nurses.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.080
AGAIN.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.440
We’ve seen this exact conversation included
in The Conjuring, Annabelle and now Annabelle

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.440
Comes Home.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.640
At least this time we get to see what happens
after that.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:34.610
Ed takes the doll as he and Lorraine begin
a long drive home.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:38.090
Lorraine says they might get lost and she’ll
wake up in California, that could also be

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:41.910
a reference to the fact that the Annabelle
doll was in California in the last movie chronologically,

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.040
or maybe a clue that they’ll be headed there
in the future.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.180
The car breaks down near a cemetery, and Ed
hops out to inspect it.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.170
Lorraine hears a voice say, “I like your
doll”.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:53.661
Annabelle Higgins, also known as Janice, says
this exact line when breaking into John and

00:00:53.661 --> 00:00:55.360
Mia’s home in Annabelle.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.560
"I like your dolls."

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.790
One of the things I’ll be talking about
in this video is how the demon that is attached

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:08.080
to the Annabelle doll learns new tricks from
each home he stays in.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.180
Imitating the Higgins adopted daughter is
just one of them.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.781
As the pastor from The Conjuring helps Ed
and Lorraine secure the doll, a number of

00:01:14.781 --> 00:01:18.700
supernatural occurrences take place, one of
which is the clocks moving backwards.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:22.940
Much later on in the film, the character Danielle
sees a TV screen that shows a feed of her

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:23.940
a couple seconds into the future.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.810
So I’m thinking that time manipulation could
be a new ability that the demon, Malthus,

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:28.810
has picked up.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:32.230
This may or may not be related to Lorraine’s
ability to see past and future events, as

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:36.320
showcased in The Conjuring 2, or the TV that
seems to show programs related to what’s

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.170
about to happen next in the original Annabelle.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:41.869
Judy’s babysitter Mary Ellen goes to the
grocery store to prepare a cake for her birthday

00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:45.100
and at the end of one of the isles there is
a comic book display with four covers that

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:48.009
we can see, Swamp Thing, The Demon, Detective
Comics and Batman.

00:01:48.009 --> 00:01:52.659
The Demon is obviously there because the antagonists
of The Conjuring Universe are demons, but

00:01:52.659 --> 00:01:56.610
another interesting note is that all four
comics are DC. James Wan, who directed The

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:00.530
Conjuring 1 and 2 and David F Sandberg, who,
as you know, directed Annabelle: Creation,

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:02.920
both went on to make DC comic book movies.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:06.509
I haven’t seen these movies, but I have
heard they sometimes link back with an Annabelle

00:02:06.509 --> 00:02:07.509
reference.

00:02:07.509 --> 00:02:10.739
Mary Ellen’s friend Daniela shows up at
the house and finds a bell, and she asks if

00:02:10.739 --> 00:02:12.239
this is a spirit bell.

00:02:12.239 --> 00:02:15.359
When the spirits are unleashed later, all
the bells ring like crazy.

00:02:15.359 --> 00:02:17.870
This is one of those tricks that Malthus picked
up over the years.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.989
In Annabelle: Creation, Esther Mullins is
bed ridden and uses a similar bell to request

00:02:21.989 --> 00:02:25.360
help, which the demon takes advantage of to
scare these two girls.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.660
When Daniela sneaks into the Warren Artifact
Room for the first time everything we will

00:02:40.669 --> 00:02:43.469
come to know about the lore of this movie
is setup.

00:02:43.469 --> 00:02:47.489
Outside of Malthus, there are, at the very
least, three other spirits from the Warrens’

00:02:47.489 --> 00:02:49.159
past cases that are set free.

00:02:49.159 --> 00:02:52.389
Daniela touches the book on the The Black
Shuck, which if you don’t know the legend

00:02:52.389 --> 00:02:55.389
is a ghostly black dog that could be found
in the UK.

00:02:55.389 --> 00:02:58.390
Some have said it’s a demon, some have said
it’s an omen of death.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:02.769
It’s not clear if the book is the artifact
in this case, or the taxidermied dog seen

00:03:02.769 --> 00:03:06.489
in the background, but I’m guessing it’s
the book, because that’s what she touches.

00:03:06.489 --> 00:03:09.579
In the study later, when they are snooping
into the case files, it refers to the Black

00:03:09.579 --> 00:03:13.200
Shuck as a hellhound from St. Mary’s Cemetery
in England.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.159
Later we see the box that the info from this
case is kept in, and the label says February

00:03:17.159 --> 00:03:20.950
1966, which predates both The Conjuring and
Annabelle.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.049
Another object she touches is the bag of coins.

00:03:23.049 --> 00:03:25.939
The case file we later see for this is a case
called The Fairy Man.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:28.919
OK, I was kidding when I said they should
make a Conjuring movie on the tooth fairy,

00:03:28.919 --> 00:03:31.999
but turns out they’ve gone ahead and pulled
it off.

00:03:31.999 --> 00:03:35.579
This one is an ancient Greek legend about
the mythological Charon said to ferry the

00:03:35.579 --> 00:03:38.219
souls of the dead away from the land of the
living.

00:03:38.219 --> 00:03:41.900
The coins seen over the eyes of all the victims
are a reference to Charon’s obol, and it

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:45.540
was seen as a bribe for him to carry over
the soul and prevent it from drifting back

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:46.719
to the world of the living.

00:03:46.719 --> 00:03:50.090
When Daniela later invades the case file for
this, she shows a picture of a victim that

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:53.640
looks like Mary Ellen and says they could
be sisters -- this is the doppelganger like

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:57.369
woman in the coffin that Mary Ellen must pry
the Annabelle doll away from at the end.

00:03:57.369 --> 00:04:01.269
Then, there’s the wedding dress, and thought
its not said by name in Annabelle Comes Home,

00:04:01.269 --> 00:04:04.519
it’s based on the legend: The Haunted Wedding
Dress of Anna Baker.

00:04:04.519 --> 00:04:08.400
This legend is about a girl from the 1940s
who met a bitter and miserable death after

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.790
her father didn’t allow her to marry the
man who she’d fallen in love with.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:15.439
Judy explains that this dress haunts people
and causes them to become violent, which is

00:04:15.439 --> 00:04:18.849
what happens later that night to Daniela,
after the ghost of the bride pins her and

00:04:18.849 --> 00:04:22.880
does that throw up black substance in her
mouth thing -- the same thing that got Janice

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.530
possessed in Annabelle: Creation.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:28.659
So other than Malthus, those are the main
three evil spirits that get released in Annabelle

00:04:28.659 --> 00:04:32.979
Comes Home, but there a few others that I
believe got out as well -- some of which you

00:04:32.979 --> 00:04:35.229
may find familiar.

00:04:35.229 --> 00:04:37.990
Once Malthus is out, bad things start to happen.

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:41.919
That afternoon someone knocks on the door,
Mary Ellen opens it to find that it’s Bee,

00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:45.389
the deceased daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Mullins
from Annabelle: Creation and the form that

00:04:45.389 --> 00:04:47.460
the demon uses to trick them later on.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.110
One of the notes left for the girls says “Miss
me?”

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:53.361
Later on when Daniela is back in the Artifact
Room, the typewriter says “Miss me” over

00:04:53.361 --> 00:04:54.361
and over.

00:04:54.361 --> 00:04:57.949
The idea of leaving notes comes from Bee,
who used to leave her Dad notes when she wanted

00:04:57.949 --> 00:05:01.520
to play Hide and Seek, and the phrase miss
me, is something that the demon used to terrorize

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:03.720
the nurses from the opening of The Conjuring.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:07.000
The scene where Judy is attacked by the Wedding
Dress Woman in her room is very reminiscent

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.889
of a scene from The Nun, where the demon circles
around the outside of the room, then appears

00:05:10.889 --> 00:05:12.140
and charges forward.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:23.319
Whenever she walks by a picture frame, she
causes it to fall, but when she walks by the

00:05:23.319 --> 00:05:26.169
cross, it flips over into a Satanic cross.

00:05:26.169 --> 00:05:29.430
Later on, if you pay attention to the game
show on the TV, the contestant is a young

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:34.180
girl who wins a Raggedy Ann doll, so the actual
doll that the Annabelle doll is based on continues

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:37.099
the streak of appearing as an easter egg in
each movie.

00:05:37.099 --> 00:05:41.389
That night after Judy is in bed, Daniela heads
home, but realizes she still has the keys

00:05:41.389 --> 00:05:45.400
to the Warrens’ Artifact Room, so she sneaks
back in to try to contact her father one more

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.400
time.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.010
She thinks she’s made contact, but it’s
really just the demon posing as her father

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:50.010
to scare her.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:53.639
When it screams at her, the form of her dad
is missing one eye, perhaps another trick

00:05:53.639 --> 00:05:56.920
that Malthus picked up from Esther Mullins
that he adds to his arsenal.

00:05:56.920 --> 00:06:01.389
Meanwhile, Mary Ellen pours herself a glass
of milk, which the demon promptly destroys.

00:06:01.389 --> 00:06:02.389
We get it dude!

00:06:02.389 --> 00:06:03.389
You don’t like skim!

00:06:03.389 --> 00:06:06.389
The Ferryman also starts to torment her, by
rolling a bunch of coins at her?

00:06:06.389 --> 00:06:08.560
Wow man, I wish my demons gave me free money.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:12.110
But things get real when she sees the two
coins near the ceiling on the dark, because

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:15.639
anyone who’s seen the original Annabelle
may know that this is how Malthus sneaks up

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:18.220
on you by climbing on the ceiling and the
pouncing down on you.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:24.340
This is about when the air yeeting begins.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:29.020
Mary Ellen gets Air Yeeted across the floor
downstairs, and Judy is fast asleep upstairs.

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:32.439
Before I mentioned that there may be another
familiar spirit that gets released from the

00:06:32.439 --> 00:06:35.949
Artifact Room, because the way that Judy gets
pulled down on her bed is very reminiscent

00:06:35.949 --> 00:06:39.930
of the attacks issued by Bathsheba -- the
witch that the Warrens defeat in The Conjuring.

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:44.340
"It's not funny anymore, I'm trying to sleep,
please don't pull my feet."

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:53.740
But that isn’t all, because the music box
that Bathsheba is stored inside appears in

00:06:53.759 --> 00:06:57.940
the climax scene in the study, where it can
be seen sitting in the background before somehow

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:01.330
appearing back in the Artifact Room at the
end of the movie.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:05.010
But back to Judy’s room for a moment -- the
light projector is knocked down and four shadows

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.650
appear on the wall, one for each color of
light.

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:11.749
The first is the shape of the Annabelle doll,
then Bee, then the adult Annabelle Higgins

00:07:11.749 --> 00:07:15.610
and the last one is Malthus, which is the
first we see of him in his true form during

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:16.610
this movie.

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:20.069
As I mentioned, Malthus has picked up some
alternate forms and tricks along the way,

00:07:20.069 --> 00:07:23.979
from the farmhouse in Annabelle: Creation,
to the apartment in Annabelle, to the nurses’

00:07:23.979 --> 00:07:27.819
home in The Conjuring, but apparently he’s
also been to the Wizarding World of Harry

00:07:27.819 --> 00:07:31.759
Potter, because when he tries to suck out
Judy’s soul through her face, which is exactly

00:07:31.759 --> 00:07:34.120
how the Dementors suck your soul out in Harry
Potter.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.940
Together, the three girls are able to contain
the evil once again, but before I end this

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:40.990
video, I have one more lingering question
I’d like to answer.

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:44.669
The whole idea of this movie is that Judy
has this young babysitter that makes the mistake

00:07:44.669 --> 00:07:48.779
of letting a friend open up the Artifact Room
-- but what happened Judy's Grandmother that

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.210
stays over and takes care of her in The Conjuring?

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.340
"Mom it's me, is Judy OK?

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:56.460
Can you go check please?

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:59.060
**** Mom just check, please!!"

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:01.100
"You gonna tell me what's going on?"

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:02.110
"No!"

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:05.349
We know Annabelle Comes Home takes place between
The Conjuring and The Conjuring 2, because

00:08:05.349 --> 00:08:08.509
the music box that they acquired at the end
of the first one is there on the shelf, but

00:08:08.509 --> 00:08:11.770
the toy they acquired from The Conjuring 2
isn’t there yet.

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:15.809
Actually it doesn't 100% make sense because
this scene takes place in '68, so I think

00:08:15.809 --> 00:08:20.090
the one year later text in Annabelle Comes
Home just means one year after The Conjuring.

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:24.310
So Annabelle Comes Home must take place in
1971 or 1972.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:26.199
So what happened to Georgiana in that one
year?

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:29.830
It’s possible they just fired her after
this whole incident took place.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:31.260
"Judy!"

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:32.200
"Nana!"

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.140
"Judy open the door!"

00:08:33.149 --> 00:08:34.149
"Mom!!"

00:08:34.149 --> 00:08:35.480
"Judy!"

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:36.500
"Help!"

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:37.540
"Judy, open up--"

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:38.180
"What is it?"

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:40.420
"What's going on in there?"

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:42.440
...but I like to think they were still on
good terms.

00:08:42.449 --> 00:08:46.030
Georgiana was getting up there in age, and
it’s possible that she could have passed

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:47.030
on.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.320
Maybe her ghost is still present in the house.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.779
It’s never explained in Annabelle Comes
Home what caused Judy to overcome her fear

00:08:51.779 --> 00:08:56.000
of ghosts, giving her the courage to follow
the spirit of Father Michael Morrissey (that’s

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.480
the guy she sees that her school) in order
to recover the key and get back the Annabelle

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:03.360
doll -- but she does reiterate a line that
Mary Ellen had told her earlier: “maybe

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:04.740
not all ghosts are bad.”

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:09.130
I like to think she might have realized this
by encountering or remembering Georgiana’s

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:10.560
ghost somewhere along the way.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:14.660
That wraps up this trilogy of Things You Missed
in Annabelle, but click the playlist on the

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:16.630
left to see my other Conjuring Universe episodes.

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:20.880
And, we’ve got a new mainline Conjuring
movie on the way very soon -- so make sure

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:25.760
you’re subscribed to CZsWorld for new horrors
every week, ring that deathbell for notifications

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:27.940
and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:29.639
Assuming we both survive.

